### Bash Script to Deny Destructive 'rm -rf' Commands

Source: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks

This Bash script, executed by a `PreToolUse` hook, reads tool input from stdin. It denies the tool call if the command contains `rm -rf`, otherwise it exits silently to allow normal permission flow.

```bash
#!/bin/bash
# .claude/hooks/block-rm.sh
COMMAND=$(jq -r '.tool_input.command')

if echo "$COMMAND" | grep -q 'rm -rf'; then
  jq -n '{
    hookSpecificOutput: {
      hookEventName: "PreToolUse",
      permissionDecision: "deny",
      permissionDecisionReason: "Destructive command blocked by hook"
    }
  }'
else
  exit 0  # no decision; normal permission flow applies
fi
```

