### Allow Tool Use with User Permission (TypeScript)

Source: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/user-input

Implement a `canUseTool` callback to prompt the user for permission to use a tool, allowing them to grant access once or always, persisting permissions for future use.

```TypeScript
canUseTool: async (toolName, input, { suggestions = [] }) => {
  const choice = await askUser(`Allow ${toolName}?`, ["once", "always", "no"]);

  if (choice === "always") {
    const persist = suggestions.filter(
      (s) => s.destination === "localSettings"
    );
    return {
      behavior: "allow",
      updatedInput: input,
      updatedPermissions: persist
    };
  }
  if (choice === "once") {
    return { behavior: "allow", updatedInput: input };
  }
  return { behavior: "deny", message: "User declined" };
};
```

