### Commands

Source: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/interactive-mode

Users can access all available commands in Claude Code by typing "/", which reveals built-in commands, bundled and user-authored skills, and commands from plugins and MCP servers. The list can be filtered by typing letters after "/". Not all built-in commands are visible to every user, as some depend on the platform or plan.

### Create a new session ID when resuming

Source: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/cli-reference

Use the `--fork-session` flag with `--resume` or `--continue` to create a new session ID instead of reusing the original when resuming a session.

```bash
claude --resume abc123 --fork-session
```

--------------------------------

### Continue Session with query() and continue: true in TypeScript

Source: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/sessions

Pass `continue: true` in the options for subsequent `query()` calls to resume the most recent session on disk, providing the agent with previous context.

```typescript
import { query } from "@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk";

// First query: creates a new session
for await (const message of query({
  prompt: "Analyze the auth module",
  options: { allowedTools: ["Read", "Glob", "Grep"] }
})) {
  if (message.type === "result" && message.subtype === "success") {
    console.log(message.result);
  }
}

// Second query: continue: true resumes the most recent session
for await (const message of query({
  prompt: "Now refactor it to use JWT",
  options: {
    continue: true,
    allowedTools: ["Read", "Edit", "Write", "Glob", "Grep"]
  }
})) {
  if (message.type === "result" && message.subtype === "success") {
    console.log(message.result);
  }
}
```

